WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
[ YouTube Learning ]

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.300
Wouldn’t you love creating

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.700
ENGAGING presentations for your students?

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.000
Presentations that will make your students

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.240
fall in love with the topic?

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:11.600
I’m Ganesh,

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.320
I’m the founder of Don’t Memorise

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:14.520
and in this video,

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:15.640
I will teach you

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.700
the basics of creating Google Slides

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.440
in your Google Classroom!

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:23.480
[ Don't Memorise intro music ]

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:25.860
After you click on a particular class,

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.060
you can click on the Classwork tab!

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.320
This is your topic,

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.560
and this is the material within the topic.

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:34.940
This topic already has a Google Doc file,

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.160
and now say you want to add a Google Slides

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.220
presentation to it.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:40.320
To do that,

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.600
you can then click on the

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.160
3 vertical dots next to

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.160
the same material within the topic,

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:47.160
and click on Edit.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:49.080
Just like we did with Docs,

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.040
you could either ADD

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.040
an existing Google Slides Presentation

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.220
or CREATE one.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.840
Let’s try creating one by clicking here.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:58.760
And that opens a new

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.760
Google Slides presentation for you.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.500
It’s really easy for anyone

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.400
to create a presentation here.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.820
First, let’s give the presentation a name...

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:11.340
You could then add a nice title

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:12.640
to your first slide

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:13.900
so that your students know

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:15.860
what the presentation is all about.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:17.460
And by clicking here,

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:18.580
you could also see the

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:20.580
various themes available to you

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:22.620
Let’s pick this one,

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.200
and we can instantly see that it looks better.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:27.760
You can also make these texts

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.760
appear in an animated way!

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:31.740
You can click on this text box,

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.740
go to Insert,

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.500
and select animation.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:39.300
By default, this text will fade in on click.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:41.900
To get a preview of how this will appear,

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:43.260
you can click on play...

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:44.960
and then click on the screen.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.680
That’s how the text will appear.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:51.460
You can also make it Fly in from the left.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:53.540
You can see the preview again!

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:56.560
Let’s give this second object an effect too.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.760
You can select the object...

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:00.760
Click on ‘Add animation’...

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:03.700
and you can make it fly in from the right.

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:05.980
You can now begin the presentation

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:07.140
by clicking here.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:08.900
On your first click,

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:10.460
you will see this text,

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.460
and on your second click,

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:13.820
you will see this one appear.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:16.180
That’s how easy it is!

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:17.720
And as teachers,

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:20.220
we often want to show videos to our students

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:21.920
during presentations right?

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.500
Can we do that here?

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:25.180
Absolutely!

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:27.460
Let’s first add a NEW slide...

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.980
We just click on Insert

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:31.420
and then on Video.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:34.780
You could add a video using any of the 3 ways.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.180
You could search on YouTube,

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:39.960
or you could use a link that we already have,

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.400
or you could also upload a video

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.400
you have in your Google Drive Folder.

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.520
Let me quickly show it to you.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.120
I search for a youtube video,

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:52.200
select the relevant video,

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:54.200
and then click on Select.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:56.560
You will see the video here.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.260
Many times, we don’t really want to show

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.060
the entire video to the students.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:03.800
So using the Timing option here,

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:05.700
we can only select the part

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.320
that we really wish to share with students.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:10.840
And if you just want to share the animation,

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.380
and not the voice over,

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:13.600
you can even choose to

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:15.940
‘Mute the audio’ by clicking here.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:18.340
So that’s how you can add a video

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:19.500
to your presentation.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.100
But hold on,

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:23.100
the whole thing gets way better.

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:26.360
You could use Slides to give live presentations

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:28.360
to your students by clicking here.

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:31.600
You can also send the presentation directly

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.560
to all your students by clicking on the

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:34.760
Share button here.

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:37.080
Let’s present now!

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:39.880
And one important thing you will need

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:41.880
when you are giving a presentation is a Pointer.

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:44.460
Clicking on the Pointer option below

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.900
will help you point to certain objects or

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:48.160
areas on your slide.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.960
You also have the feature to add Captions

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.640
when you are presenting your Slides.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:54.940
Let’s try this out for fun.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:58.040
We can position the text at the top

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:00.040
and select the size as Large.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:02.440
Now let me start talking.

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:07.060
“We can learn more about this concept

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.360
using animation”...

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:10.080
Amazing right?

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:12.220
And now I come to what I think is one of the

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:14.220
coolest features of Google Slides.

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:15.740
The QNA section!

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.400
Clicking here will lead you to

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.480
an audience tool

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:20.960
where you can generate a link

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.480
to share with your students.

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:24.180
Using this link,

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:25.880
your students or fellow teachers

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:27.380
could ask you questions!

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:29.860
Let’s try this out.

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:32.840
Once the link is shared with the students,

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:34.840
they will see a screen like this one,

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:36.760
where they can ask their questions.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:40.140
They could even ask it anonymously too.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.160
Once the question is asked,

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:44.160
you will see it here in this section!

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:47.160
I know you’d be surprised to know that

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:50.260
so many options exist with this one simple tool.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:52.120
If you practice and

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:53.900
get better at Google Slides,

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:56.240
then you could share your presentation

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:58.220
not only with your students but

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:00.000
also with the rest of the world.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:01.980
Like most Google Products,

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:03.800
you can use Google Slides on

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:06.020
any smartphone, laptop or tablet.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:08.620
You can even edit it while you are offline

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:11.220
and it will sync changes once you go online.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.960
You would have realised that it’s so easy

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:15.960
and so much fun to teach your students online.

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:17.820
In the next video,

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:19.660
I will teach you how you could create

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:21.760
quizzes and assignments for your students

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.480
on Google Classroom.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:24.980
See you there!

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:32.820
[ #TeachFromAnywhere ]

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:35.600
[ YouTube Learning ]

